{"id":"n-20261017-9qwb18","category":"gaming","display_title":"Esports Player Banned Over Bug Bites","display_title_he":"שחקן אלקטרוני הורחק מטורניר בשל עקיצות חרקים","short_summary":"Pro Super Smash Bros. player Jason 'Mew2King' Zimmerman was barred from a Texas tournament after social media posts about severe bug bites raised health concerns.","english_level":"C1","words":481,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/Wes_Copeland.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","credit":"Datagod · CC BY-SA 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wes_Copeland.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"IGN","domain":"ign.com","url":"https://www.ign.com/articles/super-smash-bros-player-mew2king-banned-from-tournament-after-bug-bites-spark-health-concerns","title":"Super Smash Bros. Player Mew2King Banned From Tournament After Bug Bites Spark Health Concerns","published_at":"2026-10-16T21:54:09.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-16T21:54:09.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-17T06:04:37.364Z","quality_score":8,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["In the high-stakes world of competitive esports, professional gamers often face intense scrutiny regarding their performance, physical stamina, and mental focus. However, an unprecedented situation recently unfolded surrounding veteran Super Smash Bros. player Jason Zimmerman, widely known by his handle “Mew2King.” Zimmerman found himself unexpectedly barred from participating in a major fighting game tournament after publishing social media posts concerning a severe bug infestation in his home and a corresponding skin condition. What began as a casual inquiry for medical advice quickly morphed into a public health debate within the gaming community, culminating in his swift disqualification from the event.","The controversy erupted when Zimmerman posted a series of photographs and message threads on Twitter/X, detailing alarming physical symptoms. He described experiencing noticeably swollen, puffy, and reddened hands, musing whether the affliction stemmed from relentless hours playing Super Smash Bros. Melee with the character Fox or from incessant insect bites in his residence. Subsequent images shared by the player depicted his right leg covered in painful red welts. Zimmerman revealed that such severe biting incidents had been recurring almost weekly throughout the year, noting that he had suffered approximately one hundred bites across his entire body just two months prior. He cited these appalling living conditions as a primary catalyst for his planned relocation from Ohio to California.","As the posts circulated rapidly online, observers and fans voiced immediate apprehension regarding Zimmerman’s health and sanitary environment. Numerous commentators speculated that the player was contending with an extensive bed bug infestation. Given the notorious tendency of bed bugs to hitchhike in luggage and apparel to establish infestations in new venues, community members strongly advised Zimmerman against traveling on commercial aircraft or checking into hotels. The overwhelming sentiment was that embarking on a trip while suffering from an active infestation posed a credible risk of contaminating public transport and hospitality facilities.","The mounting online discourse caught the attention of organizers behind Xtreme Fighters Showdown 2026, the competitive tournament Zimmerman was scheduled to attend in Texas. Prioritizing the safety and hygiene of attendees, the event’s Chief Executive Officer, operating under the moniker M333, issued an official statement on Twitter/X announcing Zimmerman's exclusion. The executive explained that management had politely informed Mew2King that he would be unable to attend or compete due to a self-reported health concern. Emphasizing that the health and overall wellbeing of participants remained the organization's utmost priority, the tournament proceeded without the legendary Smash veteran.","Following the tournament’s decision, Zimmerman removed the viral posts from his social media account and refrained from making further public statements on the matter. This bizarre episode adds to a string of unusual, viral incidents that have recently captured the attention of the competitive gaming sphere. While esports organizers routinely manage logistical hurdles and player conduct issues, public health and hygiene considerations have increasingly surfaced as unexpected operational challenges during live offline gatherings."],"facts":[{"fact":"Professional Super Smash Bros. player Jason 'Mew2King' Zimmerman was banned from the Xtreme Fighters Showdown 2026 (XFS 2026) tournament in Texas.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Zimmerman posted photos on Twitter/X showing swollen hands and red, painful-looking bumps on his right leg, which he attributed to bug bites in his home or playing SSBM Fox.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Zimmerman stated he suffers from weekly bug bites and had around 100 bites on his body two months prior, which influenced his decision to move from Ohio to California.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Fans expressed concern about a potential bed bug infestation and warned Zimmerman against flying or staying in hotels to prevent spreading them.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"XFS CEO M333 issued a public statement barring Zimmerman from attending or competing in the tournament for event safety and attendee wellbeing.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Zimmerman subsequently deleted the tweets about his condition and provided no further public updates.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"high-stakes","lemma":"high-stakes","pos":"adjective","he":"בעל סיכון או סכום גבוה","name":false},{"text":"world","lemma":"world","pos":"noun","he":"עולם","name":false},{"text":"competitive","lemma":"competitive","pos":"adjective","he":"תחרותי","name":false},{"text":"esports","lemma":"esports","pos":"noun","he"